<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Disabled is asserted; Outputs OFF; Fast/Slow/Stop Status shown but Alarms disabled]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OFF-SCAN (EnableIn is False) STATUS
============================================================
Handle "NO MODE" Selection using the standard P_Mode AOI (EnableInFalse Routine, false scan required!).

NOTE:  IN ORDER TO AVOID USING AN "AFI" (which will generate a routine verify warning),
THIS RUNG USES AN XIC of Cfg_PCmdClear, followed by an XIO of the SAME BIT
to ensure P_Mode is SCANNED FALSE ("NO MODE").

THIS IS NOT DEAD CODE AND MUST APPEAR EXACTLY AS SHOWN FOR PROPER OPERATION!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)XIO(Cfg_PCmdClear)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration still needs to happen, even when device is disabled.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTU(PCmd_RunFast)OTU(PCmd_RunSlow)OTU(PCmd_Stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(OCmd_RunFast) OTU(OCmd_RunSlow) OTU(OCmd_Stop) OTU(OCmd_Bypass) OTU(OCmd_Check) ,OTU(MCmd_Disable) OTU(MCmd_Enable) OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Override Command is set to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[ 
Since we're not processing Operator Commands, we're not READY for them either!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Rdy_RunFast) OTU(Rdy_RunSlow) OTU(Rdy_Stop) OTU(Rdy_Bypass) OTU(Rdy_Check) ,OTU(Rdy_Disable) OTU(Rdy_Enable) OTU(Rdy_Reset) OTU(Rdy_ResetAckAll) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Show the Motor Feedback as "Invalid".  If the Motor Feedback IS valid,
this value will be overwritten by one of the next three rungs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(6,Val_Fdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Motor Status bits show the state of the motor,
regardless of Mode, EVEN IF OFF-SCAN!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) XIC(Inp_SlowRunFdbk) XIO(Inp_FastRunFdbk) XIC(Cfg_UseRunFdbk) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) XIC(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) ]OTE(Sts_RunningSlow)MOV(3,Val_Fdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Motor Status bits show the state of the motor,
regardless of Mode, EVEN IF OFF-SCAN!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) XIO(Inp_SlowRunFdbk) XIC(Inp_FastRunFdbk) XIC(Cfg_UseRunFdbk) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) XIC(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) ]OTE(Sts_RunningFast)MOV(2,Val_Fdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Motor Status bits show the state of the motor,
regardless of Mode, EVEN IF OFF-SCAN!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIO(Inp_SlowRunFdbk) XIO(Inp_FastRunFdbk) XIC(Cfg_UseRunFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_UseRunFdbk) ] ,XIC(Inp_Sim) XIO(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) XIO(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) ]OTE(Sts_Stopped)CLR(Val_Fdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset the fault condition and simulation / command retrigger timers.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[RES(Wrk_FastT)RES(Wrk_SlowT)RES(Wrk_StopT)RES(Wrk_SimRunFastT)RES(Wrk_SimRunSlowT)RES(Wrk_SimStopT);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Outputs are cleared when Disabled (EnableInFalse).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Wrk_RunFast)OTU(Wrk_RunSlow)OTU(Out_RunFast)OTU(Out_RunSlow)OTU(Out_StartFast)OTU(Out_StartSlow)OTU(Out_Stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Show the motor as Disabled and Not Ready, not Available, and with no
Maintenance Bypass breadcrumb.
Clear remaining Status bits.
Show the enumerated motor command as NONE.
Show the enumerated motor status as DISABLED.
Show the enumerated motor fault status as NONE.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTL(Sts_Disabled) OTL(Sts_NotRdy) OTU(Sts_Available) OTU(Sts_MaintByp) ,OTL(Nrdy_NoMode) OTU(Nrdy_Disabled) OTU(Nrdy_CfgErr) OTU(Nrdy_Intlk) ,OTU(Nrdy_Perm) OTU(Nrdy_OperPrio) OTU(Nrdy_Fail) OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) ,OTU(Sts_StartingFast) OTU(Sts_StartingSlow) OTU(Sts_Stopping) ,CLR(Val_Cmd) MOV(33,Val_Sts) CLR(Val_Fault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the Alarms and the Notify Status, and show the Alarms Inhibited breadcrumb.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Alm_FailToStart) OTU(Alm_FailToStop) OTU(Alm_IntlkTrip) OTU(Alm_IOFault) ,OTU(Sts_FailToStart) OTU(Sts_FailToStop) OTU(Sts_IntlkTrip) OTU(Sts_IOFault) ,OTL(Sts_AlmInh) CLR(Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED SOURCE / QUALITY VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality for Input / Output values / status (SrcQ_IO)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MOV(1,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIO(Cfg_HasRunFdbk) MOV(2,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(9,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality for primary values / status (SrcQ)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(20,SrcQ);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Normal Scan: control / monitor two-speed motor]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_Motor2Spd:  PROCESS -- TWO SPEED MOTOR
============================================================
Revision 3.1-02 Release  2014-09-30:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V1.x, V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib.  Added Cfg_AllowLocal, Cfg_OperStopPrio,
Cfg_HasOvldObj. Using P_Alarm V3.0, P_Mode V3.0.
V3.0-01  2013-07-30:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-02  2013-09-03:  Modified to ensure Out_Stop always pulses
whenever a stop command is received, regardless of run
feedback state.  Modified Parameter descriptions.
V3.0-03  2013-09-10:  Corrected modification above for operation
in simulation and for all start, stop and not-ready conditions.
Modified default Parameter values.
V3.0-04  2013-10-30:  Corrected Parameter descriptions and default
configuration values for alarms only.
V3.0-05  2014-06-12:  Allow Operator retrigger of Stop command.
V3.1-00  2014-07-08:  Modified to use P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.1; added
Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_Xxxxx), source/quality values (SrcQ).
Modified to consistently use alias tag names
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Resolved held "Stopping" status. Exposed fail timers
ACC/PRE  (read-only). Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and
reset logic. Using P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.1-01.
V3.1-02  2014-09-30:  Unchanged, but using P_Alarm V3.1-02.
============================================================
This Instruction controls and monitors a two-speed motor and provides:

*  Monitoring of fast/slow run feedback, display of actual motor status
*  Detection of Failure to Start, Failure to Stop
*  Monitoring of Permissive conditions to allow starting (separate for fast and slow)
* Monitoring of Interlock conditions to stop / prevent starting
* Simulation, providing feedback of a working motor while disabling outputs
* Monitoring of I/O communication faults
* Alarms for Fail to Start, Fail to Stop, Interlock Trip, I/O Fault
* "Available" status for use by automation logic to know whether motor
can be controlled by other objects.

Modes are provided by a P_Mode AOI instance.
Alarms are provided by P_Alarm AOI instances.
Modes of operation: Operator, Program, Override, Maintenance, Hand
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag)LOWER(Cfg_FastText,Cfg_SlowText)LOWER(Inf_Lib,Inf_Type);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MODE PROCESSING
============================================================
This rung handles received Mode Inputs and Commands:

NOTE:  All Commands for Mode, Alarm are aliased directly to the
corresponding Commands in the contained P_Mode and P_Alarm AOIs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles simple First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONFIGURATION PROCESSING
============================================================
If the device is configured to not HAVE device feedback input (engineer),
it cannot be USE the feedback for fail checking (maintenance).

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Add Cfg_AllowLocal.  Cannot allow  #####
#####  local start/stop  if run feedback does not exist to monitor for it.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Cfg_HasRunFdbk)OTU(Cfg_UseRunFdbk)OTU(Cfg_AllowLocal);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These rungs get Configuration data (such as timer presets) and distribute as needed.
Note that some Configuration data are used directly in-place.

Enter the time (in seconds) for the motor to successfully start (or change speed) before declaring a fault.
Enter the time (in seconds) for the motor to successfully stop before declaring a fault.
Enter the time (in seconds) to pause stopped when changing directions.

If the timer preset calcuated wraps negative (more than 2.14... million seconds), then use a default
limit value and report Bad Configuration.  Note that a negative timer preset will fault the controller!!!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[MUL(Cfg_FailToStartT,1000,Wrk_FastT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_FastT.PRE.31) MOV(2147483647,Wrk_FastT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_FailToStopT,1000,Wrk_StopT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_StopT.PRE.31) MOV(2147483647,Wrk_StopT.PRE) ] OTE(Err_Timer) ,MOV(Wrk_FastT.PRE,Wrk_SlowT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_ChangeSpdT,1000,Wrk_ChangeSpdT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_ChangeSpdT.PRE.31) CLR(Wrk_ChangeSpdT.PRE) OTE(Err_Pause) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Enter the time (in seconds) to echo back the desired state when running in simulation

Handle timer preset invalid values as above.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MUL(Cfg_SimFdbkT,1000,Wrk_SimRunSlowT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_SimRunSlowT.PRE.31) CLR(Wrk_SimRunSlowT.PRE) OTE(Err_Sim) ,MOV(Wrk_SimRunSlowT.PRE,Wrk_SimRunFastT.PRE) MOV(Wrk_SimRunSlowT.PRE,Wrk_SimStopT.PRE) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung generates a summary Bad Config status, simply an OR of the individual bits provided above
(in the Configuration handling section).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Err_Timer) ,XIC(Err_Pause) ,XIC(Err_Sim) ,[XIC(FailToStart.Sts_Err) ,XIC(FailToStop.Sts_Err) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Sts_Err) ,XIC(IOFault.Sts_Err) ] OTE(Err_Alarm) ]OTE(Sts_Err);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
RUN FEEDBACK DETERMINATION
============================================================
If the motor is being simulated or has no run feedback, use the Sim Timers to provide
"fake" feedback signals based on the simulation time to start and time to stop.

If the motor is NOT being simulated and it HAS and IS USING run feedbacks
(slow and fast), use the states of the run feedback inputs to determine the motor state.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(Inp_Sim) ,XIO(Cfg_UseRunFdbk) ] [XIC(Wrk_SimRunSlowT.DN) OTL(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) OTU(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_SimRunFastT.DN) OTU(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) OTL(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) ,[XIC(Wrk_SimStopT.DN) ,XIC(Wrk_ChangeSpdT.DN) ] OTU(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) OTU(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) ] ,XIO(Inp_Sim) XIC(Cfg_UseRunFdbk) [XIC(Inp_SlowRunFdbk) OTL(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) ,XIO(Inp_SlowRunFdbk) OTU(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) ,XIC(Inp_FastRunFdbk) OTL(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) ,XIO(Inp_FastRunFdbk) OTU(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) ] ,XIC(Sts_Hand) XIO(Cfg_UseRunFdbk) OTU(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) OTU(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Val_Fdbk is the current state of the device feedback, as seen on the AOI's Inputs:
0 = Stopped
1 = Running Fast
2 = Running Slow
3 = Invalid]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) [XIO(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) CLR(Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) MOV(2,Val_Fdbk) ] ,XIC(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) [XIO(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) MOV(3,Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) MOV(6,Val_Fdbk) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
INTERLOCK / PERMISSIVE BYPASS / CHECK COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Bypass Command bypasses the Bypassable Permissives and Interlocks.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OCmd_Bypass)OTU(OCmd_Bypass)OTL(Wrk_Bypass);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Check Command enables checking of ALL
Permissives and Interlocks (cancels the bypass).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OCmd_Check)OTU(OCmd_Check)OTU(Wrk_Bypass);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the internal Bypass flag is set, Bypassable Interlocks and Permissives ARE BYPASSED.
Bypassing is ACTIVE if Bypass selected OR in Maintenance Mode,
or in Override Mode if Override Bypassing is configured.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Sts_Bypass) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Sts_Ovrd) XIC(Cfg_OvrdPermIntlk) ]OTE(Sts_BypActive);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Maintenance Bypass function is active, display the Maintenance Bypass
Indicator (triangle symbol) on the graphic symbol.  Bypass functions are:
*  Interlock / Permissive Bypass function is enabled
*  Motor HAS run feedback designated by engineer, but
maintenance has selected to NOT USE run feedback]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_Bypass) ,XIC(Cfg_HasRunFdbk) XIO(Cfg_UseRunFdbk) ]OTE(Sts_MaintByp);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ready for Interlock / Permissive Bypass if not bypassed.
Ready to cancel Bypass (resume checking) if bypassed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Rdy_Bypass) ,XIC(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Rdy_Check) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE DISABLE/ENABLE COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Disable Command disables the Device.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_Disable)OTU(MCmd_Disable)XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)OTL(Wrk_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Enable Command cancels the Disable and enables the Device.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_Enable)OTU(MCmd_Enable)XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)OTU(Wrk_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the internal Disabled flag is set, the motor is DISABLED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Disabled)OTE(Sts_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ready to Disable device if in Maintenance Mode and device is NOT Disabled.
Ready to Enable device if in Maintenance Mode and device IS Disabled.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)[XIO(Wrk_Disabled) OTE(Rdy_Disable) ,XIC(Wrk_Disabled) OTE(Rdy_Enable) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM RESET COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
This rung handles the Alarm Reset Input and Commands
and the "Reset and Ack All" Operator Command.

This rung processes received Reset Commands from:

1.  The Operator via HMI Operator Command, or
2.  Higher-level strategies via Program Command
3.  Pushbuttons or other block via Input
4.  Resets initiated by other device Operator Commands (if configured to do so)
and forwards the Reset to ALL Alarms and latched Shed conditions.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_Reset) ,[XIC(OCmd_RunFast) ,XIC(OCmd_RunSlow) ,XIC(OCmd_Stop) ] XIC(Cfg_OCmdResets) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) [OTL(PCmd_FailToStartAck) ,OTL(PCmd_FailToStopAck) ,OTL(PCmd_IntlkTripAck) ,OTL(PCmd_IOFaultAck) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Reset) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(Inp_Reset) ][OTL(FailToStart.PCmd_Reset) OTL(FailToStop.PCmd_Reset) OTL(IntlkTrip.PCmd_Reset) OTL(IOFault.PCmd_Reset) ,XIC(Sts_FailToStart) RES(Wrk_FastT) RES(Wrk_SlowT) ,XIC(Sts_FailToStop) RES(Wrk_StopT) ,OTU(Nrdy_OperPrio) OTU(Nrdy_Fail) ,[XIO(Inp_IOFault) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ] OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MOTOR START / STOP COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Motor is NOT READY TO RUN if:
* Interlocks are not OK and not bypassed;
* Non-bypassable Interlocks are not OK;
* Permissives are not OK and not bypassed,
or Non-Bypassable Permissives are not OK, 
and the motor is not already starting or running;
* There's an I/O failure and the motor is NOT being simulated;
* The motor has a Fail to Start or Fail to Stop that has not been reset;
* The motor is disabled by Maintenance.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Nrdy_NoMode)[XIC(Sts_Disabled) OTE(Nrdy_Disabled) ,XIC(Sts_Err) OTE(Nrdy_CfgErr) ,[XIO(Inp_IntlkOK) XIO(Sts_BypActive) ,XIO(Inp_NBIntlkOK) ] [[XIC(Wrk_RunFast) ,XIC(Wrk_RunSlow) ] OTE(Sts_IntlkTrip) ,OTE(Nrdy_Intlk) ] ,[XIO(Inp_FastPermOK) XIO(Inp_SlowPermOK) XIO(Sts_BypActive) ,XIO(Inp_FastNBPermOK) XIO(Inp_SlowNBPermOK) ] XIO(Sts_StartingFast) XIO(Sts_RunningFast) XIO(Sts_StartingSlow) XIO(Sts_RunningSlow) OTE(Nrdy_Perm) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) XIO(Inp_Sim) OTE(Sts_IOFault) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnIOFault) OTL(Nrdy_IOFault) ]OTE(Wrk_NotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MOTOR START / STOP COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Motor is NOT READY TO RUN if:
* Interlocks are not OK and not bypassed;
* Non-bypassable Interlocks are not OK;
* Permissives are not OK and not bypassed,
or Non-Bypassable Permissives are not OK, 
and the motor is not already starting or running;
* There's an I/O failure and the motor is NOT being simulated;
* The motor has a Fail to Start or Fail to Stop that has not been reset;
* The motor is disabled by Maintenance.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_NotRdy) ,XIC(Nrdy_OperPrio) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) ]OTE(Sts_NotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The motor is AVAILABLE to be run by automation if it is in PROGRAM
Mode and the "Not Ready" status is cleared.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Prog)XIO(Sts_NotRdy)OTE(Sts_Available);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If we're not timing an HMI or programmed Start or Stop,
and there's no sealed-in fail-to-start or fail-to-stop,
and if Local Start/Stop Control is permitted,
and if we are using run feedback (not in simulation),
detect a local start or stop transition and track state with it.
(Don't track the Start if conditions do not allow the motor to run.)

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  NEW RUNG.  Added Cfg_AllowLocal, check for local start/stop  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Sts_StartingFast)XIO(Sts_StartingSlow)XIO(Sts_Stopping)XIO(Sts_FailToStart)XIO(Sts_FailToStop)XIC(Cfg_AllowLocal)XIC(Cfg_UseRunFdbk)XIO(Inp_Sim)[XIC(Inp_FastRunFdbk) XIO(Sts_NotRdy) OTL(Wrk_RunFast) ,XIC(Inp_SlowRunFdbk) XIO(Sts_NotRdy) OTL(Wrk_RunSlow) ,XIO(Inp_FastRunFdbk) XIO(Inp_SlowRunFdbk) OTU(Wrk_RunFast) OTU(Wrk_RunSlow) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These next several rungs, in priority order, determine whether
the Motor should be running slow, running fast, or stopped.

If a Motor RUN SLOW command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override State is RUN SLOW, mark the Motor to RUN SLOW.
Permissives must be OK or bypassed to run the Motor (Interlocks are checked below...).
(Modes are mutually exclusive, thus handling the priority.)

#####  V3.0-02  2013-09-10:  Modified to ensure Out_StartFast always pulses whenever  #####
#####  a start command is received, regardless of run feedback state.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_RunSlow) OTU(OCmd_RunSlow) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) OTL(Wrk_Retrigger) RES(Wrk_SimRunSlowT) ] ,XIC(PCmd_RunSlow) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_RunSlow) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,4) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ][XIC(Inp_SlowPermOK) ,XIC(Sts_BypActive) ]XIC(Inp_SlowNBPermOK)[XIC(Wrk_RunFast) OTL(Wrk_ChangeSpd) ,XIO(Wrk_RunSlow) OTL(Wrk_Retrigger) RES(Wrk_SimRunSlowT) ,OTL(Wrk_RunSlow) OTU(Wrk_RunFast) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Motor RUN FAST command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override State is RUN FAST, mark the Motor to RUN FAST.
Permissives must be OK or bypassed to run the Motor (Interlocks are checked below...).
(Modes are mutually exclusive, thus handling the priority.)

#####  V3.0-02  2013-09-10:  Modified to ensure Out_StartSlow always pulses whenever  #####
#####  a start command is received, regardless of run feedback state.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_RunFast) OTU(OCmd_RunFast) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) OTL(Wrk_Retrigger) RES(Wrk_SimRunFastT) ] ,XIC(PCmd_RunFast) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_RunFast) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,3) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ][XIC(Inp_FastPermOK) ,XIC(Sts_BypActive) ]XIC(Inp_FastNBPermOK)[XIC(Wrk_RunSlow) OTL(Wrk_ChangeSpd) ,XIO(Wrk_RunFast) OTL(Wrk_Retrigger) RES(Wrk_SimRunFastT) ,OTL(Wrk_RunFast) OTU(Wrk_RunSlow) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Motor STOP command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override State is STOP,
mark the Motor TO STOP (from running slow or fast).

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Operator STOP Priority  #####
#####  V3.0-02  2013-09-10:  Modified to ensure Out_Stop always pulses whenever  #####
#####  a stop command is received or the motor goes "not ready",  #####
#####  regardless of run feedback state.  #####
#####  V3.0-05 2013-06-12:  Modified to use "Retrigger" function for Oper and Maint (for de-energize only).  #####
#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01 2014-08-29:  Resolved held "Stopping" status.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Stop) OTU(OCmd_Stop) [[XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Sts_Oper) ] ,XIC(Cfg_OperStopPrio) XIO(Sts_Oper) XIO(Sts_Maint) OTL(Nrdy_OperPrio) ] ,[XIC(PCmd_Stop) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Stop) ,NOP() ] ,XIO(PCmd_RunSlow) XIO(PCmd_RunFast) XIO(Cfg_PCmdClear) ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,1) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ,XIC(Sts_NotRdy) ][[[XIC(Wrk_RunSlow) ,XIC(Wrk_RunFast) ] OTL(Wrk_ChangeSpd) ,ONS(Wrk_NotRdyONS) ] OTL(Wrk_Retrigger) RES(Wrk_SimStopT) ,OTU(Wrk_RunSlow) OTU(Wrk_RunFast) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Higher Priority: HAND always beats Oper, Prog, Ovrd, Maint:
If in Hand, have the Motor follow the Run Feedbacks.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_Hand) ,XIC(S:FS) XIO(Sts_NotRdy) ][XIC(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) XIO(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) OTL(Wrk_RunSlow) OTU(Wrk_RunFast) ,XIO(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) XIC(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) OTU(Wrk_RunSlow) OTL(Wrk_RunFast) ,[XIO(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) XIO(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) XIC(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) ] OTU(Wrk_RunSlow) OTU(Wrk_RunFast) ]OTU(Wrk_ChangeSpd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MOTOR SPEED CHANGE TIMING
============================================================
On a speed change (fast to slow or slow to fast), this timer determines
how long to leave both outputs OFF (both contactors open) before
turning on the "other" speed output (energizing the "other" contactor).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_ChangeSpd)[TON(Wrk_ChangeSpdT,?,?) ,XIC(Wrk_ChangeSpdT.DN) OTU(Wrk_ChangeSpd) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MOTOR START SIMULATION AND FAIL TO START DETECTION
============================================================
If the motor SHOULD BE RUNNING FAST, run a Fast Run Timer to check for Fail to Start, and run a
Simulation Timer to provide simulated run feedback if needed.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30: Moved Maintenance check two rungs down and  #####
#####  feedback check to this rung in order  to allow timer  #####
#####  use for newly added Local Start / Stop detection function.  #####

@@@@@  The TON on the second branch is doubled to ensure it goes  @@@@@
@@@@@  the same scan it is enabled if its preset is zero.  @@@@@]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_RunFast)XIO(Wrk_ChangeSpdT.TT)[NEQ(Val_Fdbk,2) TON(Wrk_FastT,?,?) ,TON(Wrk_SimRunFastT,?,?) TON(Wrk_SimRunFastT,?,?) ,XIC(Wrk_SimRunFastT.DN) OTU(Wrk_Retrigger) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the motor SHOULD BE RUNNING SLOW, run a Slow Run Timer to check for Fail to Start, and run a
Simulation Timer to provide simulated run feedback if needed.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30: Moved Maintenance check to next rung and  #####
#####  feedback check to this rung in order  to allow timer  #####
#####  use for newly added Local Start / Stop detection function.  #####

@@@@@  The TON on the second branch is doubled to ensure it goes  @@@@@
@@@@@  the same scan it is enabled if its preset is zero.  @@@@@]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_RunSlow)XIO(Wrk_ChangeSpdT.TT)[NEQ(Val_Fdbk,3) TON(Wrk_SlowT,?,?) ,TON(Wrk_SimRunSlowT,?,?) TON(Wrk_SimRunSlowT,?,?) ,XIC(Wrk_SimRunSlowT.DN) OTU(Wrk_Retrigger) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Start Timer times out and the motor run feedback (or simulated feedback) never showed up,
show the motor as "FAILED TO START"

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30: See comments on previous two rungs.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_FastT.DN) ,XIC(Wrk_SlowT.DN) ]XIO(Sts_Maint)OTE(Sts_FailToStart);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MOTOR STOP SIMULATION AND FAIL TO STOP DETECTION
============================================================
If the motor SHOULD BE STOPPED, run a Stop Timer to check for Fail to Stop, and run a
Simulation Timer to provide simulated run feedback off (stop feedback) if needed.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30: Moved Maintenance check to next rung and  #####
#####  feedback check to this rung in order  to allow timer  #####
#####  use for newly added Local Start / Stop detection function.  #####

@@@@@  The TON on the second branch is doubled to ensure it goes  @@@@@
@@@@@  the same scan it is enabled if its preset is zero.  @@@@@]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RunFast)XIO(Wrk_RunSlow)[NEQ(Val_Fdbk,0) TON(Wrk_StopT,?,?) ,TON(Wrk_SimStopT,?,?) TON(Wrk_SimStopT,?,?) ,XIC(Wrk_SimStopT.DN) OTU(Wrk_Retrigger) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Stop Timer times out and the motor run feedback (or simulated feedback) never showed "stopped",
show the motor as "FAILED TO STOP"

#####  V3.0-00 2013-06-30 : See comments on previous rung.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_StopT.DN)XIO(Sts_Maint)OTE(Sts_FailToStop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SHED ON FAULT LOGIC
============================================================
This rung handles latching in of conditions which are configured to cause
motor to shed (de-energize).

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_FailToStart)XIC(Cfg_ShedOnFailToStart)OTL(Nrdy_Fail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE COMMAND ENUMERATED VALUE
============================================================
Val_Cmd is the command currently being processed:
0 = None
1 = Stop
2 = Start Fast
3 = Start Slow]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Cmd) ,XIO(Wrk_RunFast) XIO(Wrk_RunSlow) [XIC(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_Retrigger) ] MOV(1,Wrk_Cmd) ,XIC(Wrk_RunFast) [XIO(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_Retrigger) ] MOV(3,Wrk_Cmd) ,XIC(Wrk_RunSlow) [XIC(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) ,XIO(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_Retrigger) ] MOV(4,Wrk_Cmd) ,MOV(Wrk_Cmd,Val_Cmd) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OUTPUT GENERATION
============================================================
If the motor is NOT SIMULATED and NOT DISABLED, generate the
appropriate outputs for the motor.
If the motor is not faulted and not in hardwired control, energice Out_RunSlow if the
motor should be running slow.
Also, energize Out_StartSlow until we get feedback that the motor is running slow.

Likewise nergice Out_RunFast if the motor should be running fast.
Also, energize Out_StartFast until we get feedback that the motor is running fast.

If the motor should be stopped and is not in hardwired control and the feedback shows the motor
is NOT stopped, or if the motor is Faulted, energize the Out_Stop output to stop the motor.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)[XIO(Sts_NotRdy) XIO(Wrk_ChangeSpdT.TT) [XIC(Wrk_RunSlow) [OTE(Out_RunSlow) ,[XIO(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_Retrigger) ] OTE(Out_StartSlow) ] ,XIC(Wrk_RunFast) [OTE(Out_RunFast) ,[XIO(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_Retrigger) ] OTE(Out_StartFast) ] ] ,[XIO(Wrk_RunSlow) XIO(Wrk_RunFast) [XIC(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_Retrigger) ,XIC(Wrk_NotRdy) ] ,XIC(Wrk_ChangeSpdT.TT) ] OTE(Out_Stop) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE STATUS GENERATION
============================================================
If the motor is in HAND and HAS NO RUN FEEDBACKS, its state is meaningless;
turn off ALL the Sts_xxx states!!!!!

If the motor is commanded to run slow (Output on) and the feedbacks don't yet show it running slow,
the motor is STARTING SLOW.

If the motor is commanded to run slow (Output on) and the feedbacks show it running slow,
the motor is RUNNING SLOW.

If the motor is commanded to run fast (Output on) and the feedbacks don't yet show it running fast,
the motor is STARTING FAST.

If the motor is commanded to run fast (Output on) and the feedbacks show it running fast,
the motor is RUNNING FAST.

If the motor is commanded to stoop (Outputs off) and the feedbacks still show it running (either speed),
the motor is STOPPING.

If the motor is commanded to stop (Output off) and the feedbacks show it has stopped,
the motor is STOPPED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Sts_Hand) ,XIC(Cfg_UseRunFdbk) ][XIC(Wrk_RunSlow) [XIO(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) OTE(Sts_StartingSlow) ,XIC(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) OTE(Sts_RunningSlow) ] ,XIC(Wrk_RunFast) [XIO(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) OTE(Sts_StartingFast) ,XIC(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) OTE(Sts_RunningFast) ] ,XIO(Wrk_RunSlow) XIO(Wrk_RunFast) [[XIC(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) ] OTE(Sts_Stopping) ,XIO(Wrk_SlowRunFdbk) XIO(Wrk_FastRunFdbk) OTE(Sts_Stopped) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED SOURCE / QUALITY VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality for Input / Output values / status (SrcQ_IO)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MOV(1,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIO(Cfg_HasRunFdbk) MOV(2,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(9,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality for primary values / status (SrcQ)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MOV(SrcQ_IO,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Cfg_HasRunFdbk) XIO(Cfg_UseRunFdbk) MOV(18,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Val_Sts is the current device status, as determined by this AOI,
based on its knowledge of commands executed and feedback.
(This is the status that should be monitored by, for example, FT Historian.)
0 = Powerup / Unknown
1 = Stopped
3 = Running Fast
4 = Running Slow
7 = Stopping
9 = Starting Fast
10 = Starting Slow
33 = Device Disabled

Val_Fault is the current device fault status, as determined by this AOI,
based on its knowledge of commands executed and feedback.
(This is the fault status that should be monitored by, for example, FT Historian.)
0 = None
16 = Fail to Start
17 = Fail to Stop
32 = I/O Fault (from Input)
34 = Configuration Error

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Sts) CLR(Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_Stopped) MOV(1,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_RunningFast) MOV(3,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_RunningSlow) MOV(4,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Stopping) MOV(7,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_StartingFast) MOV(9,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_StartingSlow) MOV(10,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) MOV(16,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_FailToStop) MOV(17,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) MOV(32,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_Disabled) MOV(33,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Err) MOV(34,Wrk_Fault) ,MOV(Wrk_Sts,Val_Sts) MOV(Wrk_Fault,Val_Fault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OPERATOR COMMAND READIES
============================================================
Ready to Start if in Operator Manual, Stopped, and Permissives and Interlocks are OK.

Ready to Stop if in Operator Manual and (Running or Starting).

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Operator Stop Priority logic.  #####
#####  V3.0-05  2014-06-12:  Modified to allow operator retrigger stop.  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_NotRdy)[XIO(Sts_NotRdy) ,XIC(Cfg_OCmdResets) ][[XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] [[XIC(Sts_Stopped) XIO(Wrk_ChangeSpdT.TT) ,XIC(Sts_RunningFast) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) XIC(Sts_RunningSlow) ] [XIC(Inp_SlowPermOK) ,XIC(Sts_BypActive) ] XIC(Inp_SlowNBPermOK) OTE(Rdy_RunSlow) ,[XIC(Sts_Stopped) XIO(Wrk_ChangeSpdT.TT) ,XIC(Sts_RunningSlow) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) XIC(Sts_RunningFast) ] [XIC(Inp_FastPermOK) ,XIC(Sts_BypActive) ] XIC(Inp_FastNBPermOK) OTE(Rdy_RunFast) ] ,[XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Cfg_OperStopPrio) ] XIO(Sts_Stopping) OTE(Rdy_Stop) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM PROCESSING
============================================================
Pass the Cfg_PCmdClear configuration down to each P_Alarm instance.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(FailToStart.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(FailToStop.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(IntlkTrip.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(IOFault.Cfg_PCmdClear);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="42" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The various alarms are ALWAYS allowed to Exist (Cfg_HasXxxAlarm can be 1), EXCEPT:
* If the motor DOES NOT HAVE RUN FEEDBACK, the Fail to Start and Fail to Stop
alarms will never occur and should not exist.  (If feedback exists, 
the Fail alarms must be allowed to exist.)

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added PCfg_AllowExist on P_Alarm 3.0.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTL(IntlkTrip.PCfg_AllowExist) OTL(IOFault.PCfg_AllowExist) ,XIC(Cfg_HasRunFdbk) OTE(FailToStart.PCfg_AllowExist) OTE(FailToStop.PCfg_AllowExist) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="43" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Motor Failed to Start Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(FailToStart);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="44" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Motor Failed to Stop Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(FailToStop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="45" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Interlock Trip Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(IntlkTrip);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="46" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle I/O Fault Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(IOFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="47" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If ANY alarm is Disabled, Inhibited or Suppressed, set the Alarm Inhibit
summary status bit (which puts the "I" box on the graphic symbol).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(FailToStart.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(FailToStop.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(IOFault.Sts_AlmInh) ]OTE(Sts_AlmInh);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="48" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
NOTIFICATION VALUE
============================================================
Indicate the current alarm notification level as the max of any of the alarms,
and set the low-order bit for reset or ack required:
0 = Not in alarm, acknowledged
1 = Not in alarm, unacknowledged or reset required
2 = Low severity alarm, acknowledged
3 = Low severity alarm, unacknowledged
4 = Medium severity alarm, acknowledged
5 = Medium severity alarm, unacknowledged
6 = High severity alarm, acknowledged
7 = High severity alarm, unacknowledged
8 = Urgent severity alarm, acknowledged
9 = Urgent severity alarm, unacknowledged

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Separated Reset Reqd functions from Val_Notify  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(FailToStart.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(FailToStart.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(FailToStop.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(FailToStop.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(IOFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(IOFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,[XIC(FailToStart.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(FailToStop.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(IOFault.Val_Notify.0) ] OTE(Wrk_Notify.0) ,MOV(Wrk_Notify,Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="49" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung identifies:
* if a latched Shed condition requires a reset in order to run the motor;
* if that reset or any alarm reset or other reset is required; and
* if any reset or acknowledge from the operator is required.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx); split from Val_Notify logic (above).  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(FailToStart.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(FailToStop.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(IOFault.Rdy_Ack) ] ,[XIC(FailToStart.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(FailToStop.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(IOFault.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(Nrdy_OperPrio) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) XIO(Sts_IOFault) ] OTE(Rdy_Reset) ]OTE(Rdy_ResetAckAll);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Prescan" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Clear Ownership, clear "lurking" Commands]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
PRESCAN (POWERUP) HANDLING
============================================================
On Prescan, set the Ownership to NO OWNER (0).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(PSet_Owner)CLR(Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTU(PCmd_RunFast)OTU(PCmd_RunSlow)OTU(PCmd_Stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(OCmd_RunFast) OTU(OCmd_RunSlow) OTU(OCmd_Stop) ,OTU(OCmd_Bypass) OTU(OCmd_Check) OTU(MCmd_Disable) OTU(MCmd_Enable) ,OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Override Command is set to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the latched Shed faults.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Nrdy_OperPrio)OTU(Nrdy_Fail)OTU(Nrdy_IOFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[All Outputs are de-energized on Prescan.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Wrk_RunFast)OTU(Wrk_RunSlow)OTU(Out_RunFast)OTU(Out_RunSlow)OTU(Out_StartFast)OTU(Out_StartSlow)OTU(Out_Stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[On Prescan, clear the following:
Val_Cmd (no command active)
Val_Fdbk (device position not determined)
Val_Sts (device status powerup / unknown)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Val_Cmd)CLR(Val_Fdbk)CLR(Val_Sts);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_40"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_16"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_20"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="P_Alarm"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_12"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="P_Mode"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
